          "content": "Think!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.14,
            0.797,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "**Q. In Fig. 2.20, we have** $\\angle AOB = \\angle BOC = \\angle COD = \\angle DOE = \\angle EOF = \\angle FOG =$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.168,
            0.419,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "∠**GOH =** ∠HOI= . Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.195,
            0.398,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Each of the angles = 22.5º"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.223,
            0.881,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "As the straight angle of 180º is divided into eight equal parts so each of the right angles will be of measure $\\frac{180^{\\circ}}{8}=22.5^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.303,
            0.239,
            0.319
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.33,
            0.778,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "**Q.1. Find the degree measures of the following angles using your protractor.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.358,
            0.356,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": "Ans. $\\angle  IIIJ = \\angle  III  = 47^{\\circ}$ ∠GHK = ∠IHJ = 23º ∠IHJ = ∠JHI = 108º"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.442,
            0.881,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Find the degree measures for the angles given below. Check if your paper protractor can be used here!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.488,
            0.498,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "Ans. $\\angle  IIIJ = 42^{\\circ}, \\quad \\angle  IIIJ = 116^{\\circ}$ No, paper protractor cannot work here."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.544,
            0.87,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "**Q.4. How can you find the degree measure of the angle given below using a protractor?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.572,
            0.693,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Measure of marked angle = 360º – Measure of unmarked angle $360^{\\circ}-100^{\\circ}=260^{\\circ}$ Try other ways to find the marked angle"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.643,
            0.785,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "**Q.5. Measure and write the degree measures for each of the following angles:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.673,
            0.161,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.696,
            0.224,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "a. $8 0 ^ { \\circ }$ b. $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }$ c. $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ d. $1 3 0 ^ { \\circ }$ e. $1 3 0 ^ { \\circ }$ f. $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.814,
            0.833,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "**Q.6. Find the degree measures of** ∠**BXE,** ∠**CXE,** ∠**AXB and** ∠**BXC.** Ans. $\\angle \\mathrm{BXE} = 115^{\\circ}$ ∠ $\\mathrm{CXE}=85^{\\circ}$ $\\angle \\mathrm{AXB} = 65^{\\circ}$ $\\angle BXC = 30^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.869,
            0.633,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": "**Q.7. Find the degree measures of** ∠**PQR,** ∠**PQS and** ∠**PQT.** Ans. $\\angle PQR = 45^{\\circ}$ $\\angle PQS = 100^{\\circ}$ 2 $\\angle P Q T = 1 5 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
